  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -1,
  "section_notes": "The package keeps the 5% 55 °C heat-test cap but converts exceedance into corrective action plus oversight rather than a sales ban, blocks publication of individual-company per-model failure rates to the general public while routing complete per-model results to purchasers and regulators, and stretches the retrofit deadline to six years — the three biggest Northwind wins. Halcyon secured customer access to complete per-model results (its HC-1 red line) and a 36-month suppression lead time (HC-2), but the S5 mandatory recall at 8 incidents/100,000 would catch its Ember 8 (9.9) and the S1 reporting regime is strict (24h reporting, all incidents, 3-day customer notice). S3/S4 land inside the acceptable ranges, and S2 is weakened only through the no-sales-stop consequence, not through its limit or disclosure terms."
 },
